   "unmapped": [
    "Adversary flips binary preference labels (strong adversary observing selected actions and true label); C bounds the number of flipped labels",
    "Regret is the average dueling regret sum_t 2r*(x_t,a*_t) - r*(x_t,a_t) - r*(x_t,b_t)",
    "Link function derivative lower bounded by kappa (c_mu) over all feature differences and parameters"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In each round $t \\in [T]$, the agent observes the context information $x_t$ ... selects two actions, $a_t$ and $b_t$. ... $\\PP(a \\succ b| x) = \\sigma\\big(r^*(x,a)-r^*(x,b)\\big)$ ... an adversary will see both the choice of the agent and the true feedback. Based on the information, the adversary can decide whether to corrupt the binary feedback or not. ... $\\sum_{t=1}^{T}c_t \\le C$."
  },
