    "number": "Theorem 8",
    "quote": "For any algorithm $\\textbf{Alg}$ and any $d, C, T \\ge \\max\\{ (4d^2)/25,dC\\}, \\kappa>0$, there exists an instance of dueling bandit with link function $\\sigma$, satisfying $\\dot\\sigma(...) \\ge \\kappa$, such that the regret of $\\textbf{Alg}$ over $T$ rounds is $\\Omega\\big((d\\sqrt{T}+ dC)/\\kappa\\big)$."
